          "settings": {
            "heading": "When may additional mouth-opening support be relevant?",
            "toc_label": "When it may help",
            "anchor": "when"
          }
        },
        "text_1": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>You may want to discuss guided mouth-opening exercises with a qualified healthcare professional if:</p>"
          }
        },
        "checklist_1": {
          "type": "checklist",
          "settings": {
            "items": "Your mouth opening is restricted.\nYou experience tightness or stiffness when opening your mouth.\nLimited movement makes eating, speaking or oral hygiene more difficult.\nYou need help following a consistent mouth-opening exercise routine.",
            "columns": "1"
          }
        },
        "text_2": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Whether device-assisted exercises are appropriate depends on your individual needs and mouth-opening status.</p>"
          }
        },
        "link_1": {
          "type": "link",
          "settings": {
            "label": "Find an OSMF Specialist Doctor",
            "url": "/pages/find-osmf-specialist"
          }
        },
        "chapter_2": {
          "type": "chapter",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Why a structured exercise routine matters",
            "toc_label": "Why a routine matters",
            "anchor": "why-routine"
          }
        },
        "text_3": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>When mouth opening is restricted, regular exercises may form part of a broader rehabilitation plan. A structured approach can help you build consistency, follow guidance and monitor progress over time.</p>"
          }
        },
        "checklist_2": {
          "type": "checklist",
          "settings": {
            "items": "Build a regular exercise routine.\nApproach movement gradually rather than forcefully.\nFollow professional guidance and review progress when advised.\nConsistency matters more than intensity.",
            "columns": "1"
          }
        },
        "chapter_3": {
          "type": "chapter",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How the MARCEL® MOFlex Device fits into care",
            "toc_label": "How it works",
            "anchor": "how-it-works"
          }
        },
        "text_4": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>The MARCEL® MOFlex Device may be considered as an optional adjunct for selected individuals who need additional support with mouth-opening exercises. It is intended to support functional rehabilitation as part of a broader care plan. It does not replace:</p><ul><li>Professional assessment or personalised clinical advice</li><li>The broader care plan recommended for you</li><li>Mouth-opening exercises and follow-up guidance</li></ul><p>It is associated with the functional-rehabilitation component of the MARCEL OMR Therapy™ Advance programme, where appropriate. It is not required by every patient.</p>"
          }
        },
        "link_2": {
          "type": "link",
          "settings": {
            "label": "Explore MARCEL OMR Therapy™ Advance",
            "url": "/pages/advance-kit"
          }
        },
        "chapter_4": {
          "type": "chapter",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What the device is designed to support",
            "toc_label": "What it supports",
            "anchor": "supports"
          }
        },
        "checklist_3": {
          "type": "checklist",
          "settings": {
            "items": "Guided mouth-opening exercise routines\nA gradual, controlled approach to movement\nConsistency with rehabilitation exercises\nFunctional improvement efforts as part of a structured care plan",
            "columns": "2"
          }
        },
        "callout_1": {
          "type": "callout",
          "settings": {
            "style": "muted",
            "icon": "info",
            "text": "<p>Individual experiences and outcomes vary. Do not expect instant results, and do not force movement to achieve a target.</p>"
          }
        },
        "chapter_5": {
          "type": "chapter",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Use and guidance",
            "toc_label": "Use and guidance",
            "anchor": "use"
          }
        },
        "checklist_4": {
          "type": "checklist",
          "settings": {
            "items": "Use the device only in accordance with the final approved instructions and advice from a qualified healthcare professional.\nBegin with comfortable movement and progress only as advised.\nDo not force movement or continue through pain.\nFollow the exercise routine recommended for your individual needs.\nClean and maintain the device according to the approved instructions.",
            "columns": "1"
          }
        },
        "chapter_6": {
          "type": "chapter",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Who may be considered for device-assisted exercises?",
            "toc_label": "Who it is for",
            "anchor": "who"
          }
        },
        "text_5": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>The MARCEL® MOFlex Device may be considered for selected individuals with restricted mouth opening, including some people with Oral Submucous Fibrosis (OSMF), based on individual assessment. It is not intended for everyone, and the decision to use it should be guided by an appropriately qualified healthcare professional.</p>"
          }
        }
